{"tool_name":"idrem","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"idrem","home":"https://github.com/phoenixding/idrem","license":"MIT","summary":"An interactive version of DREM software, which enables to integrate static protein-DNA interaction data with different types of time series data for reconstructing dynamic regulatory networks. It also allows users to interactively visualize a gene, TF, path or model-centric view of each of these data types, their interactions and their impact on the resulting model.","addition_date":"2018-06-25T09:23:50Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T13:49:39.946206Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:idrem","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"jund@cs.cmu.edu","name":"Jun Ding","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://github.com/phoenixding/idrem/blob/master/UserManual.pdf"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Database cross-mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0954"},"format":[{"term":"Data index format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3326"}]},{"data":{"term":"Gene expression data","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2603"},"format":[{"term":"Matrix format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3033"},{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]},{"data":{"term":"Pathway or network","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2600"},"format":[{"term":"Matrix format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3033"},{"term":"TSV","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3475"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Gene functional annotation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3672"},{"term":"Pathway or network prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3439"},{"term":"Pathway or network visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3083"},{"term":"Statistical modelling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3664"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Pathway or network","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2600"},"format":[{"term":"Graph format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3617"},{"term":"Matrix format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3033"}]}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"iDREM","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-EE","publication":[{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pcbi.1006019","metadata":{"abstract":"The Dynamic Regulatory Events Miner (DREM) software reconstructs dynamic regulatory networks by integrating static protein-DNA interaction data with time series gene expression data. In recent years, several additional types of high-throughput time series data have been profiled when studying biological processes including time series miRNA expression, proteomics, epigenomics and single cell RNA-Seq. Combining all available time series and static datasets in a unified model remains an important challenge and goal. To address this challenge we have developed a new version of DREM termed interactive DREM (iDREM). iDREM provides support for all data types mentioned above and combines them with existing interaction data to reconstruct networks that can lead to novel hypotheses on the function and timing of regulators. Users can interactively visualize and query the resulting model. We showcase the functionality of the new tool by applying it to microglia developmental data from multiple labs.","authors":[{"name":"Ambalavanan N."},{"name":"Bar-Joseph Z."},{"name":"Ding J."},{"name":"Hagood J.S."},{"name":"Kaminski N."}],"citationCount":26,"date":"2018-03-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"PLoS Computational Biology","title":"iDREM: Interactive visualization of dynamic regulatory networks"},"pmcid":"PMC5868853","pmid":"29538379"}],"topic":[{"term":"Data mining","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3473"},{"term":"Data visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0092"},{"term":"Function analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_1775